 east o Konab. The road requires\n4 WD that con tum slippery clay when\nwer. If you are feeling adventurous, there\nare other sink ho es in the area to explore.\nThis arventure is on the Grard Stair Case\nEscalare National Monument,\nܕܘܕܐ܀\nBOUT\nson\nKANAB\nMAGICALLY UNSPOILE\n6038\n4\'19\nEAGLE GPS 37 2.652\nSINK\n112 9 048\nHP\nTRAILS\nLANAB\nUT\nSAPP\nN\n2000\nThe\nLIFE\nADVENTURE MAP RESPECTE KANAB ABRA KANABRA! UTAH\nELEVATED','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Eagle Sink\",\n  \"distance\": \"20.75 mi\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year Round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Moderate\",\n  \"elevation\": \"5800 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.0442\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-112.1508\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"4WD\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"Yes\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"3\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"4WD\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, drive 20.75 miles East on HWY 89. After mile post 43, turn right. Cross the cattle guard and follow this road. It will Y into another road and you will be heading west. Go a short distance and watch for a T road to the left road #730. Take the T road and watch for another Y and the sign pointing to Eagle Sink right.\",\n  \"description\": \"Eagle Sink is an amazing limestone sinkhole that can be seen from the highway. This hole is approximately 160 ft. deep and is in an area with 360 views, that is worth the drive itself. Part of the area is fenced off for your safety. The rest of the area is open, don\'t go near the edge, there are a lot of loose rocks and wind gusts. You may hear a lot of birds chirping and flying in and out of the sinkhole. It is located approximately 21 miles east of Kanab. The road requires 4WD that can turn slippery clay when wet. If you are feeling adventurous, there are other sinkholes in the area to explore. This adventure is on the Grand Staircase-Escalante National Monument.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Eagle Sink is an amazing limestone sinkhole that can be seen from the highway. This hole is approximately 160 ft. deep and is in an area with 360 views, that is worth the drive itself. Part of the area is fenced off for your safety. The rest of the area is open, don\'t go near the edge, there are a lot of loose rocks and wind gusts. You may hear a lot of birds chirping and flying in and out of the sinkhole. It is located approximately 21 miles east of Kanab. The road requires 4WD that can turn slippery clay when wet. If you are feeling adventurous, there are other sinkholes in the area to explore. This adventure is on the Grand Staircase-Escalante National Monument.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"Disclaimer: \\\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads can be impassable when wet. Please respect Private Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas! Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\\\", Phone: 435.644.5033\"\n}','2023-09-22 02:50:16','2023-09-22 02:55:47'),(13,'trails',268,'FUN FOR KIDS\nRECREATION,\nin\nFUN FOR KIDS\nRECREATION\nU.S. 89\nTO SALT LAKE,\nBRYCE & ZION\n<spart\n89\n300 North\n200 North\n100 North\nHORTH\n(89)\n9\n@上\nSOMBOR CITIZEN CENTER\nHOSPITAL\nw\nCENTER STREET\n100 South\nADVENTURE MAP\n200 South\n300 Scuth\nTENNIS:\nSWIMMING POOL:\nSKATE PARK:\nHIKING:\nBASKETBALL:\nPARK:\nKANAD TRAILS\nTRAILHEAD\nELEVATION:\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 5 100 E\nSQUAW TRAIL\nDADE\nGETTING THERE:\n•\nFrom the certer of town, at the stoolight at Center and Main, go north an Main Street,\nYou will see the library, tennis couts, basketball courts, pump track and baseball fields.\n• To get to the Jacob: Hamblin pork, tum right on 300 north.\n• Go I slack and turn left on 100 east.\nUBRARY\n* For Squaw trail drive past the park to the end of the road, to the trailhead.\n• Hike north and follow the signs\n€ 의\nYES\n• The trail goes to the lop, where you can connect to a whole trail system.\n• You may download the Kanab Treils Apo to help navigate trals.\nYES\nDISCLAIMER:\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always chack local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads cre mpassable when wel. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water\nfood, sunscreen, and suppies Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your vist so\nothers may enjoy.\"\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\n450 North\n405 North\nYES\n5771 FEET\n300 North\nYES\n200 North\n100 Nort\nYES\nYES\nLess than a mile from beautiful downtown\nKanab is Jacob Hanblin Fark Here you.\ncon cool off in the splash pad play\nvoleyball, basketball or teans and then\ntake a dip in the pool. There is also a\npumpTack for bikes and scooters\nAcove the baseball fields there is\narress in Squnw Tmil, a 3-mile indirip\nhike for the family. Kcnab has the best\npark ever. The pavillion can be reservered\nfor parties through Kanab City\'s website.\nDuring the summer, you may find the farmers\nMarket or movies in the park. We have the\nbest small town Independence Day\ncelebration in the country! Celebrate\nIndependence Day in the park, The Kanah\nWay. See the Kare County Vision Center for\ninformation and maps on our hiking trails.\n200 South\nLIFE\ntread lightly! UTAH\nELEVATED\nKANE COUNTY VISITOR CENTER\n89\nLOCT\nKANAB\nMAGICALLY UNSPOILE\nU.S. 89\nWHAT\nCAPPE\nNORTH\nKANAB\nMasc. EPILE','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Fun for Kids Recreation\",\n  \"distance\": \"\",\n  \"best_season\": \"\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"\",\n  \"elevation\": \"\",\n  \"latitude\": \"\",\n  \"longitude\": \"\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From the center of town, at the stoplight at Center and Main, go north on Main Street. You will see the library, tennis courts, basketball courts, pump track, and baseball fields. To get to the Jacob Hamblin Park, turn right on 300 north and then go slack and turn left on 100 east. For the Squaw trail, drive past the park to the end of the road, to the trailhead. Hike north and follow the signs. The trail goes to the top, where you can connect to a whole trail system. You may download the Kanab Trails App to help navigate trails.\",\n  \"description\": \"Less than a mile from beautiful downtown Kanab is Jacob Hamblin Park. Here you can cool off in the splash pad, play volleyball, basketball, or tennis, and then take a dip in the pool. There is also a pump track for bikes and scooters. Above the baseball fields, there is access to Squaw Trail, a 3-mile family-friendly hike. Kanab has the best park ever. The pavilion can be reserved for parties through Kanab City\'s website. During the summer, you may find the farmers market or movies in the park. We have the best small-town Independence Day celebration in the country! Celebrate Independence Day in the park, The Kanab Way. See the Kane County Visitor Center for information and maps on our hiking trails.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Less than a mile from beautiful downtown Kanab is Jacob Hamblin Park. Here you can cool off in the splash pad, play volleyball, basketball, or tennis, and then take a dip in the pool. There is also a pump track for bikes and scooters. Above the baseball fields, there is access to Squaw Trail, a 3-mile family-friendly hike. Kanab has the best park ever. The pavilion can be reserved for parties through Kanab City\'s website. During the summer, you may find the farmers market or movies in the park. We have the best small-town Independence Day celebration in the country! Celebrate Independence Day in the park, The Kanab Way. See the Kane County Visitor Center for information and maps on our hiking trails.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"Disclaimer: \\\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads can be impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas! Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\\\" Phone: 435.644.5033\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:30:24','2023-09-22 02:31:59'),(14,'trails',269,'LOWER HACKBERRY CANYON\nSLOT CANYON HIKE\nCHIUS\nKANAB\n46.2 mi\nEAST\n89\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nADVENTURE MAP\nBEST SEASON: SPRING SUMMER FALL\nROAD:\nHIKING:\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\nothers may enjoy.\"\nMAINTAINED DIRT ROAD\n4.5 MI ROUND TRIP\nHALF DAY\nEASY\nGETTING THERE:\n• From Kanab, drive 46.2 miles East on HWY 89.\n• Just post mile post 18, turn left onto road #200, the Cottonwood Road.\nLOWER HACKBERRY CANYON\nSLOT CANYON HIKE\n• Collonwood Road can be impossible when wet\n• Drive approximately 14.7 miles and turn turn left at the sign for the Lower Fackberry Canyon.\n• Park in the parking area, put on your water shoes and head west and drop into the wash.\n• Walk through the willows on the fo nt hiking path..\n• Soon you will enter Hackberry Canyon heading west.\nThe dinosaur tracts will be at 2.1 mile, on the left bank. Then hike back.\n• Water can be murky from sediment, conditions can include quicksand and muc slicks and can\nLe Fozarcous.\n• Be aware of possible flash floods during monsoon seaso1..\nDISCLAIMER:\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads cre mpassable when wel. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water.\