ROUND\n• From the center of town at the stop light at Center and Main Street, go north on Main Street.\n• Turn right on 300 North.\n• Go 4 blocks, enter La Estancia subdivision, then turn right at the waterwheel.\n.\n• Park at the top of the street as curves.\n• Walk up the hill to the trailhead kiosk.\n• Follow the trail up the canyon.\nWatch for the sign for the Cliffs Conrector Trail on your left that takes you on top of the cliffs.\nEAST\n89\n2WD\n1.9 MILES\n3 HOURS\nDISCLAIMER:\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads cre mpassable when wet. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water\nfood, sunscreen, and suppies Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your vist so\nothers may enjoy.\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 5 100 E\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\ntread lightly!\nDIFFICULT\n6000 FEET\nTOMB CANYON TRAIL\nKanab is known for its awaseme hiking trails.\nThe Cliffs Connector Trail will take you on\ntop of the cliffs and connect into several other\nLikes: Cliffs 2. Milk Bolles, TV Tower overloak,\nK-Hill and Squaw Trail The hike starts on the\nToms Canyon Trail Once on top, you will\nhave 360° breathtaking views. Watch\nfor the sign on your left about a mile in,\ndrecting you to the Cliffs Connector Trai.\nThe trail is sleep, rocky and easy to follow\nYou will be traveling switchbacks up the ciff\nNear the top is a cif wall- it looks difficult but\nit is suprisingly easy to climb; the trail then\ngoes lell and you are 30 lee below the im\nOnce on top the trail is hard to follow.\nDowrloed the Karob Trails App to help you\nnav gale the trail system. It is recommended to\ncome down Squaw Trail.\n(92)\nCLIFFS\nCONNECTOR\nTRAIL\nDion\nLIFE\nUTAH UT\nELEVATED\nAPP\nwww.\nKASAR IRAN\nKANAB\nMOFICALLY WASPOILE\nTom\n5600\n5800\nKANAB\nWELLSPORED','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Cliffs Trail\",\n  \"distance\": \"500\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year Round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Difficult\",\n  \"elevation\": \"6000\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.0464\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-112.5244\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"2WD\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"No\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"3\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"From the center of town at the stop light at Center and Main Street, go north on Main Street. Turn right on 300 North. Go 4 blocks, enter La Estancia subdivision, then turn right at the waterwheel. Park at the top of the street as it curves. Walk up the hill to the trailhead kiosk.\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"Follow the trail up the canyon. Watch for the sign for the Cliffs Connector Trail on your left that takes you on top of the cliffs.\",\n  \"description\": \"Kanab is known for its awesome hiking trails. The Cliffs Connector Trail will take you on top of the cliffs and connect into several other trails: Cliffs 2, Milk Bolles, TV Tower Overlook, K-Hill, and Squaw Trail. The hike starts on the Tomb Canyon Trail. Once on top, you will have 360° breathtaking views. The trail is steep, rocky, and easy to follow. Near the top is a cliff wall, but it is surprisingly easy to climb. Once on top, the trail is hard to follow. Download the Kanab Trails App to help you navigate the trail system. It is recommended to come down Squaw Trail.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"Kanab is known for its <strong>awesome hiking trails</strong>. The <strong>Cliffs Connector Trail</strong> will take you on top of the cliffs and connect into several other trails: <strong>Cliffs 2, Milk Bolles, TV Tower Overlook, K-Hill, and Squaw Trail</strong>. The hike starts on the <strong>Tomb Canyon Trail</strong>. Once on top, you will have 360° breathtaking views. The trail is steep, rocky, and easy to follow. Near the top is a cliff wall, but it is surprisingly easy to climb. Once on top, the trail is hard to follow. Download the <strong>Kanab Trails App</strong> to help you navigate the trail system. It is recommended to come down <strong>Squaw Trail</strong>.\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"Disclaimer: This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads can be impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas. Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy. Kanab Visitor\'s Center: 785 100 E\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:31:09','2023-09-22 02:34:19'),(21,'trails',276,'CROSBY CANYON\nOHV\nKANAB\nto s\nMILE\n7\n57 mi\nBIG\nWATEH.\nVISITOR\nCENTER\nSMOKY\nEAST\n89\nADVENTURE MAP\nXROK\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\n9.25 mil\nBEST SEASON:\nCROSBY CANYON\nATV/4WD\nVEHICLE:\nCAMPING\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\nGETTING THERE\nMOUNTAIN\nPAGE\nYES\nYEAR ROUND\n300\nPRIMITIVE CAMPING\n4WD/ATV\n• From Konob, ake HWY 89 east 57 miles to Big Water.\n• Turn left just past mile post 7.\n• Look for the Ethan Allen Rond off of HWY 89 and turn north\n• Take road #300, the Smoky Mountain Road for 9.3 miles.\n• Watch for the Crosby Canyon sign road #231 and turn right.\n• A1 3.95 miles to the Warm Creek Canyon overlook.\n• Enjoy your day at the lake.\nROAD\ntread lightly!\nFULL DAY\nDISCLAIMER\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check loco rood and\nweather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Din roads are impassable when wel Please respect\nFrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra\nwater, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most\nareas! Do not remove or facts or deface the \'rock ort\'.\nLeave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\"\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 S 100 E\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\nMODERATE\n3717 FEET\nTake a buckrood adventure and spend\nthe day playing, jeeping, swimming,\nfishing, pooling, camping o riding one\nof many ATV rails near Crosby Canyan\nand Luke Powell\'s Wann Creek Bay.\nThe crive through Crosby Canyon\nis a beautiful gorge, with narrow Iwists\nand uras. There is evidence that it was\nunderwoler long ago. When you reach\nthe end of Crusby Canyon the diffs\nopen up to a spectatcular view of Lake\nPowell. There are many small beaches\nand peninsulas for camping, swimming\nand the fishing is the best or just st back\nrelax and enjoy the views. It is not\nrecommended to make this drive when\nroads are wet, cs it can be impassable.\n231\nLIFE\nUTAH\nELEVATED\nKANAB\nMAGICALLY UNSPEILE\nGPS 37 4.442\n-111 28.256\nCROSBY\n4 mi CANYON\nOVERLOOK\nCABLE TAKE\nUT\nAPP\nN\nLAKE POWELL\nRATUSL\nKANAB\nWALLY UNLES','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Crosby Canyon\",\n  \"distance\": \"7 miles\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year-round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Moderate\",\n  \"elevation\": \"3717 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.07442\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-111.28256\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"4WD/ATV\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"Yes\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"Full day\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"Off-road vehicle\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, take HWY 89 east 57 miles to Big Water. Turn left just past mile post 7. Look for the Ethan Allen Road off of HWY 89 and turn north. Take road #300, the Smoky Mountain Road for 9.3 miles. Watch for the Crosby Canyon sign road #231 and turn right. About 3.95 miles to the Warm Creek Canyon overlook.\",\n  \"description\": \"Take a off-road adventure and spend the day playing, jeeping, swimming, fishing, camping or riding one of many ATV trails near Crosby Canyon and Lake Powell. The drive through Crosby Canyon is a beautiful gorge, with narrow twists and turns. There is evidence that it was underwater long ago. When you reach the end of Crosby Canyon, the views open up to a spectacular view of Lake Powell. There are many small beaches and peninsulas for camping, swimming, and fishing. The fishing is especially good in this area. It is not recommended to make this drive when roads are wet, as it can be impassable.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Take a off-road adventure and spend the day playing, jeeping, swimming, fishing, camping or riding one of many ATV trails near Crosby Canyon and Lake Powell. The drive through Crosby Canyon is a beautiful gorge, with narrow twists and turns. There is evidence that it was underwater long ago. When you reach the end of Crosby Canyon, the views open up to a spectacular view of Lake Powell. There are many small beaches and peninsulas for camping, swimming, and fishing. The fishing is especially good in this area. It is not recommended to make this drive when roads are wet, as it can be impassable.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads are impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas! Do not remove or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:31:15','2023-09-22 02:34:41'),(22,'trails',277,'Bo\nU.S.89\nTO SALT LAKE,\nBRYCE & ZION\n<ACHIN\n300 North\n200 Norza\n8 sego\nOLALPUR LOGGE\n100 North Days Inn\nLITTLE\nHOLLYWOO\nTHE CAVE CAFE\nBRYCE\n(60 minuts)\nTHEYOULE\nCOWBOY\nBUNK\nHOUSE\nFREDONIA AZ\n(10m nutes)\nCEDAR MOUNTAIN\n(15 minutes)\nVest\nPIPE SPRINGS\n(25 minuts)\nKANADCHIK\nCENTER STREET\nSUNNY\nCREEK\nCOFFEE\nTHE TOW\n(10 minutes)\nFONDEROSA GROVE\n200\nRoggw\nmu..\nZION\n(30 rrinules!\nBEST FRIENDS\nANIMAL SANCTUARY\nTHE RED PUEBLO MUSEUM\n(10 minutes)\n100 Wast\n000\n215\nNORTH RIM GRAND CANYON\n90 m nutes?\nNOSTAL\nwwwww\nwww\nn\nSIRS\n100 Se