until the povement ends turn right onto Skutumpah Road #500.\nThis is a well maintained cirt road\n14.8 mi\ntread lightly!\nMODERATE\n• Continue for 14.8 miles and watch for a sign that says \"FLOOD AREA\". The trailheed parking\nis short y after on your right.\n• Follow he wash southeast to the entrance of Lick Wash.\n• The hike to Park Wash junction is 4 miles one way.\n8000 FEET\nDISCLAIMER:\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always chack local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads cre mpassable when wel. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water\nfood, sunscreen, and suppies Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your vist so\nothers may enjoy.\"\nKANAB\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 5 100 E\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\nMOFICALLY UNSPOILE\nCALON PREL\nLick Wash is a enjoyable half day\nhike in a narrow canyon lined with\nponderosa pines, douglas lis and\nbroad Navajo sendstone. It is cool\nand shady in the narrows, with little\nsnade in the broad stretches. The\ncanyon is especially beautiful in the\nfall when the eaves are changing\ncolors. This is an easy, 4 mile one\nway hike through a grovelly wash.\nYou can hike as little or as much as\nyou want, ust turn around and go\nback the way you came when your\nhave walked as much as you would\nlike. This route can be used to access\nFurk Wash and No Mans Mesa.\nDEER\nSPRINGS\nRANCH\nLIFE\nUTAH\nELEVATED\nLICK WASH\nTRAILHEAD\nN\nGPS 37 21.877\n112 11.311\nMARTINE\nUT\nAFP:\n4 mi\nPARK\nWASH\nLICK WASH\nNO\nMANS\nMESA\nKANAB\nNAGGI DISPOLED','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Lick Wash Slot Canyon\",\n  \"distance\": \"16.2 mi\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Spring, Summer, Fall\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Moderate\",\n  \"elevation\": \"8000 FEET\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.364617\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-112.188517\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"Yes\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"No\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"Half day\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"A5\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, travel east on HWY 89 for 9.5 miles and turn left onto Johnson Canyon Road. Drive 16.2 miles until the pavement ends, then turn right onto Skutumpah Road #500.\",\n  \"description\": \"Lick Wash is an enjoyable half-day hike in a narrow canyon lined with ponderosa pines, douglas lis, and broad Navajo sandstone. It is cool and shady in the narrows, with little shade in the broad stretches. The canyon is especially beautiful in the fall when the leaves are changing colors. This is an easy, 4 mile one-way hike through a gravelly wash. You can hike as little or as much as you want, just turn around and go back the way you came when you have walked as much as you would like. This route can be used to access Furk Wash and No Mans Mesa.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Lick Wash is an enjoyable half-day hike in a narrow canyon lined with ponderosa pines, douglas lis, and broad Navajo sandstone. It is cool and shady in the narrows, with little shade in the broad stretches. The canyon is especially beautiful in the fall when the leaves are changing colors. This is an easy, 4 mile one-way hike through a gravelly wash. You can hike as little or as much as you want, just turn around and go back the way you came when you have walked as much as you would like. This route can be used to access Furk Wash and No Mans Mesa.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads can be impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas! Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:32:20','2023-09-22 02:38:16'),(34,'trails',289,'MAIL DROP\nATV/HIKE\nMAIL DROP\nATV/HIKE\nMAIL\nDROP\n1,mi\nSHUNES\nHOLLOW\nWARRIORS WALK\nADVENTURE MAP\nA80\nGATE\n25\n19\n19\n1220\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nBEST SEASON:\nVEHICLE:\nHIKING:\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\n17C\nK 1250\nGETTING THERE:\n• From Konob, drive 7.8 miles north on HWY 39.\n• Just sast mile post 71, turn left onto the Hancock rood.\n• Drive 9.3 miles to the stop sign and turn loft.\n• Drive 9.1 miles and turn right on road K1250 it is also signed 3200 West.\n• Drive 2.2 o sign with road map. You can park here and unload ATV\'s.\n• The trail starts on your left. Road 10.\n• Drive approx mctly 9 miles, stay left on road 25.\n• Park at the gate and hike 1 mile to overlook.\n• Follow the wash, watch for the rack corne(stack of rocks) on your right and hike up to over ook.\nThis hike is in Canaan Mountain Wilderness, be sure to leave no trace.\nK 1245\nDISCLAIMER:\n*This ir ap and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designated reads. Dirt roads are impassable when wet. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water,\nload, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is no existent in most areas!\nDo not remove crtifacts or deface the \'ocs art\'. Leave no trace of your visit so\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\nothers may enjoy.\"\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 5 100 E\n25F\n10H\n4.49 mi 17\nROUGH\nSECTION\n17B\n4WD\n2 MILES ROUND TRIP\nHALF DAY\nYEAR ROUND\nK(1290\n25\n7.73 mi\n10\nK/1215\n10G\nHEAL\nMODERATE\n5600 FEET\nK 1287\n25\nYES\nSAND BUTTE\n10\n2.7 m\n10\n27\n2.2 mi\n20M\nMINUING\nLocols love this popular ATV end jeep ride. The\nride starts 4miles southwast of the Coral Pink\nSand Dunes State Park. The trail goes out past\nElephan Bulle, a famous landmark that looks\nlike an elephant with a trunk. The nde is in deep\nsand will aume sundstons rock sucium,\nwinding through sego brush and\njuniper res Watch in the amazing views\nof Zion National Park. The rood enes a a\nfence line. Park and hice from here. The hike is\non easy 2 miles round trip mostly in a sardy\nwash. In the early days, it was very dangerous\nfor the mail carner bringing mail from Kanab to\ndescend into Shones Creek where the sellers\nwould meet him. Later, they built a cable syston\nthat the mail conier used is lower the rail over\n300 foct clff evedoosing Rockville and\nSpringdcle to the Shunes Creek samlers\n25D\nSPRING\nK 1250\n20\nELEPHANT BUTTE\nK 1260\n20\n25\nLIFE\ntread lightly! UTAH\nFLEVATIO\n*K/1255\n20\n20\n20\n20\n(P)\nKANAB\nMOSICALLY UNSPOILE\nELEPHANT GAP\n97-991001\nCALEFAN\nUT\nAPP\nN\n4.49 mi BANDLOUNGS\nELEPHANT COVE\nSTAGING AREA\nKANAB\nMORICE DESP','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Mail Drop ATV/Hike\",\n  \"distance\": \"1 mi\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year Round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Moderate\",\n  \"elevation\": \"5600 ft\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.0461° N\",\n  \"longitude\": \"113.1584° W\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"Yes\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"Yes\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"Half Day\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"4WD\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, drive 7.8 miles north on HWY 39. Just past mile post 71, turn left onto the Hancock road. Drive 9.3 miles to the stop sign and turn left. Drive 9.1 miles and turn right on road K1250, which is also signed 3200 West. Drive 2.2 miles to a sign with a road map. You can park here and unload ATVs. The trail starts on your left, Road 10. Drive approximately 9 miles, staying left on Road 25. Park at the gate and hike 1 mile to the overlook. Follow the wash and watch for the cairn (stack of rocks) on your right to hike up to the overlook.\",\n  \"description\": \"Locals love this popular ATV and jeep ride. The ride starts 4 miles southwest of the Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park. The trail goes out past Elephant Butte, a famous landmark that looks like an elephant with a trunk. The ride is in deep sand with sandstone rock formations, winding through sagebrush and juniper trees. Enjoy the amazing views of Zion National Park. The road ends at a fence line. Park and hike from there. The hike is an easy 2 miles round trip, mostly in a sandy wash. In the early days, it was very dangerous for the mail carrier bringing mail from Kanab to descend into Shunes Creek where the sellers would meet him. Later, they built a cable system that the mail carrier used to lower the mail over a 300-foot cliff, avoiding Rockville and Springdale to reach the Shunes Creek settlers.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Locals love this popular ATV and jeep ride. The ride starts 4 miles southwest of the Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park. The trail goes out past Elephant Butte, a famous landmark that looks like an elephant with a trunk. The ride is in deep sand with sandstone rock formations, winding through sagebrush and juniper trees. Enjoy the amazing views of Zion National Park. The road ends at a fence line. Park and hike from there. The hike is an easy 2 miles round trip, mostly in a sandy wash. In the early days, it was very dangerous for the mail carrier bringing mail from Kanab to descend into Shunes Creek where the settlers would meet him. Later, they built a cable system that the mail carrier used to lower the mail over a 300-foot cliff, avoiding Rockville and Springdale to reach the Shunes Creek settlers.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"This hike is in Canaan Mountain Wilderness, so be sure to leave no trace.\",\n  \"phone\": \"435-644-5033\",\n  \"address\": \"78 5 100 E, Kanab Visitor\'s Center\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:32:27','2023-09-22 02:38:42'),(35,'trails',290,'MAMMOTH CAVE\nLAVA TUBES\nORE6\nN\n14\n-DV\n21304*\n750\n50\n$75\nADVENTURE MAP\nA+ 000\nOFF THE\nBEATEN PATE:\nBEST SEASON:\nVEHICLE:\nMAMMOTH CAVE\nLAVA TUBES\nHIKING:\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\n1923\n5.4 mi\n\"Che\nMAS CO\nGETTING THERE\nFrom Kanab drive 40 miles north on HWY 89.\n•\nTurn left onto HWY 14.\n• Travel 9,4 mie turn right on road FH50/Mommoth Road.\n• After 5.4 miles turn right on to road 1609.\n• At the T in the rood, continue straight on cad 950 for 45 miles to the trailhead.\nNOTE:\nB\nThe cave hus four crambers, the largest is to the west. At the end of the largest turmel, it muntows\nto a small opening that can be used as an exit. You will nocd a good flash light. The passage is\nabout a quarter of a mile lorg. Best explored in long pants and long sleeve shirts. Because of the\ncoolness of the cave you may want a jacket.\n9.4\nDISCLAIMER:\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dit roads are impassable when wet. Please respe\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water,\nfood, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-ex stant in most araasl\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the \'rock art\'. Leave no trace of your visit so\nothers may enjoy\nKarab Visitor\'s Center: 78 S 100 E\nLAPK\nwww.\n6.\nYES\nS\nMAY-SEPTEMBER\nALL TYPES\n2100 FT OF PASSAGES and requires you to slide through on your\nbelly, or turn arourd anc go back the\nsome way you came. Portions of the cave\ncontoir wet rocks that can be slippery.\nThis cave is frequented by seven species\nof bats. Winter visitation puts hibemaling\nkate at great risk. To provide protection for\nthem, e gate heas been insta led and is\nlocked to humans October - April.\nAccessible May September\nEASY TO MODERATE\nHALF DAY\ndama\nWELD CO\n34 135\n8060 FEET\nMammoth Cave is one of the largest love\ntubes in Utah, with over 2100 feet of\npassages and five entrances. The cave\nlooks like a big hole in the ground and\nis exciting to explore. It is extremely\ndark, everyone will need a good\nflashlight. The exit is a simull tube\nTh\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\n...\n1 mi\n1609\nto HWY 89\nLIPE\ntread lightly! UTAH\nELEVATED\n45 mi\n950\n(P\nMAMMOTH\nCAVENATIONAL\nGPS 37 34.09\n112 35.256\nTrailhead Parking Area\n10\nKANAB\nMasically UnSPOILED\nUT\nAPP\nKANAB\nNa ne','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Mammoth Cave\",\n  \"distance\": \"5.4 mi\",\n  \"best_season\": \"May-September\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Easy to Moderate\",\n  \"elevation\": \"8060 FEET\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.56941\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-112.5876\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"Accessible May-September\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"YES\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"NO\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"HALF DAY\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"ALL TYPES\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab drive 40 miles north on HWY 89. Turn left onto HWY 14. Travel 9.4 miles, turn right on road FH50/Mammoth Road. After 5.4 miles, turn right onto road 1609. At the T in the road, continue straight on road 950 for 45 miles to the trailhead.\",\n  \"description\": \"Mammoth Cave is one of the largest lava tubes in Utah, with over 2100 feet of passages and five entrances. The cave looks like a big hole in the ground and is exciting to explore. It is extremely dark, so everyone will need a good flashlight. The cave has four chambers, the largest being to the west. At the end of the largest tunnel, it narrows to a small opening that can be used as an exit. The passage is about a quarter of a mile long. Best explored in long pants and long sleeve shirts. Because of the coolness of the cave, you may want a jacket.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Mammoth Cave is one of the largest lava tubes in Utah, with over 2100 feet of passages and five entrances. The cave looks like a big hole in the ground and is exciting to explore. It is extremely dark, so everyone will need a good flashlight. The cave has four chambers, the largest being to the west. At the end of the largest tunnel, it narrows to a small opening that can be used as an exit. The passage is about a quarter of a mile long. Best explored in long pants and long sleeve shirts. Because of the coolness of the cave, you may want a jacket.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads are impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas. Do not remove artifacts or deface the \'rock art\'. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\",\n}','2023-09-10 06:32:33','2023-09-22 02:39:04'),(36,'trails',291,'MANSARD\nATV\nMANSARD\nETURIL\n100\nHOG CANYON.\n104\nHOG CANYON\n104\n24\nADVENTURE MAP\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\n7.9 mi\nBEST SEASON:\nVEHICLE:\nHIKING:\nAVERAGE TIME\nAPM\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\nEfte\n3.9 mi\nGETTING THERE\n• Fram Kanch drive 9.5 miles cast on HWY 89, just past milepost 55, turn left on Johnson Canyon Road.\n• Travel 7.5 miles to the Crocodile / Hag Canyon Trailhead on your left\n• The trail starts herind the information sign en rone 100. The mad vears latt one then through the\nwash and starts climbing uphil\n• Continue on road 100, for 3.9 miles to the Hog Conyan turn off and arr left on road 104.\nBorr\nYEAR ROUND WEATHER\nPERMITTING\nATV ONLY\n* Continue onother 79 mies on road 104. You will pass the road to Hog Canyon on the right\nContinue past the overlook tum out. DO NOT proceed past this point unless you are on an ATV.\nThe road becomes too narrow for a vehicle and there is nowhere to turn around. The last leg will\nbe a life challenging, some rock crowing is involved.\n+\n• Continue until the rood ends. The trail starts behind the Mansard sign.\nFe\n20 MILES ROUND TRIP\nHALF DAY\nTHE LAST 2 MILES\nARE CHALLENGING\nDISCLAIMER\n*The map and directions are intereed for genere, reference van ar y Aways check ocal road and\nweather osadition ». Boy >1 designales recids. Dirt roads are mpassable when wer Pause speci\nPrivale Property. Be prepares lor\'a w ceire