": \"Year-round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Difficult\",\n  \"elevation\": \"5040 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.25218\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-111.93495\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"Off the beaten path\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"Yes\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"Full day\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"4WD\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab drive 33.5 miles south on Hwy 89. Turn left after mile post 31 at the Old Paria Townsite rock marker. Drive the dirt road for approximately 5.6 miles down to the bottom of the canyon. Continue past the cemetery and park.\",\n  \"description\": \"The Paria River hike is a 22-mile adventure in southern Utah. It is accessed by heading north in the river. You can hike as much as you want and then turn around and come back the same way. The route offers beautiful scenery and some rock art, but please do not touch. Be cautious of quicksand and flash floods during the monsoon season.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>The Paria River hike is a 22-mile adventure in southern Utah. It is accessed by heading north in the river. You can hike as much as you want and then turn around and come back the same way. The route offers beautiful scenery and some rock art, but please do not touch. Be cautious of quicksand and flash floods during the monsoon season.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"Please note that this map and instructions are for general reference only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads, respect private property, and be prepared for a wilderness experience. Bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service may not be available in all areas. Do not remove or deface any artifacts or rock art, so that others may enjoy. For more information or concerns, contact the BLM Visitor Center.\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:33:02','2023-09-22 02:41:34'),(41,'trails',296,'PARIA\nTOWNSITE\nPARIA\nTOWNSITE\nBefore it burned down. OFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nLICK\nWASH\nTh\nKANAB 33.5 mi\nADVENTURE MAP\n88 O **\nSKUTUMPAH ROAD\nBEST SEASON:\nROAD:\nHIKING\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\n22 mi\nPARIA\n44\nRIVER\nMILE\nGETTING THERE:\n• From Kanab drive 33.5 miles east on HWY 89.\n• Turn left after mile [pos 31), you will see the Old Town Paria Rock marker.\n• Drive the dirt road for approximately 5.6 miles down to the bottom of the canyon.\n• Dirt roads can be impasscble when wet.\n• Those who want to hike, continue past the cemetery and park\n.\n• Pictured to the left, the rock building is accessed by heading cast across the river.\n• The Paric River Hike is accessed by heading north in the river. This is a 22 mile hike\none way. You may hike as far as you like and then turn around and come back.\nANDOR\nYEAR ROUND\nGOOD DIRT ROAD\nDISCLAIMER:\n*This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check loca road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads are in passable when wet. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water,\nfood, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non existent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the \'rock crt. Leave no trace of your visit so\nothers may enjoy.\"\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 $ 100 E\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\nNO\n22 NILES\nHALF DAY - DAY\nEASY\n6040-6800 FEET\n5.6 mi\ntread lightly!\nSTRONO\n89\nPahreah (the historic spelling of \"Puric\"!\nwas abandoned for a few years in the late\n1860\'s during the Bleckhawk war, but was\nre-occupied shortly thereafter. Repeated\nflooding and resulting loss of grazing and\nagricultural land, a result of\novergrozing cnd poor dam constuction,\nforced people to move out, and by the late\n1800\'s/early 1900\'s Not much remains bu\na few foundations and wooden fences.\nYou can see the ole cemetary that has about\n20 graves in 1930 a movie sel with a lew\nwooden buildings were stucted just beyonc\nthe parking area. Because of the beauty,\nHollywood filmed many western movies\nhere, including some scenes of the Outlaw\nJosey Wales. In 2006 the movie sel was\nsumed down by vancals\nGPS 37 15.131:\n111 56.097\nPARIA\nTOWNSITE\nCEMETARY\nP\nLIFE\nUTAH\nELEVATED\nPAVEIRIN\nUT\nAPP\nKANAB\nMAGICALLY UNEPOILED\nN\nKANAB\nKADLEY INSPE','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Paria Townsite\",\n  \"distance\": \"22 miles\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year-round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n  \"elevation\": \"6040-6800 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.25218\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-111.93495\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"Good dirt road\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"No\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"Half day to a full day\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"Car\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, drive 33.5 miles east on HWY 89. Turn left after mile 31, you will see the Old Town Paria Rock marker. Drive the dirt road for approximately 5.6 miles down to the bottom of the canyon. Dirt roads can be impassable when wet. Those who want to hike can continue past the cemetery and park. The rock building is accessed by heading east across the river. The Paria River Hike is accessed by heading north in the river. This is a 22-mile hike one way. You may hike as far as you like and then turn around and come back.\",\n  \"description\": \"The Paria Townsite, located in Utah, was once a bustling community but was abandoned due to repeated flooding and loss of grazing and agricultural land. Today, not much remains except a few foundations and wooden fences. The old cemetery, with about 20 graves, can still be seen. In the 1930s, a movie set was constructed nearby, and many western movies, including scenes from \'The Outlaw Josey Wales,\' were filmed here. Unfortunately, the movie set was burned down by vandals in 2006.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>The Paria Townsite, located in Utah, was once a bustling community but was abandoned due to repeated flooding and loss of grazing and agricultural land. Today, not much remains except a few foundations and wooden fences. The old cemetery, with about 20 graves, can still be seen. In the 1930s, a movie set was constructed nearby, and many western movies, including scenes from \'The Outlaw Josey Wales,\' were filmed here. Unfortunately, the movie set was burned down by vandals in 2006.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads are impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas! Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\",\n}','2023-09-10 06:35:55','2023-09-22 02:41:56'),(42,'trails',297,'PEEKABOO\nSLOT CANYON\nPEEKABOO\nSLOT CANYON\nNORTH\n89\nAND\nFou\nADVENTURE MAP\nA800\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nBEST SEASON:\nYEAR ROUND\nATV\nVEHICLE:\nHIGH CLEARANCE AND REQUIRED\nNOT RECOMMENDED\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\nGETTING THERE:\nAbout 9 miles north from Konab on HWY 89 between mi epost 72 and 73, you will see the turn off\nfor Peekaboo trailhead on the east light hane sidel of the rood.\n• The rood into the canyon is a deep sandy trail that\nwith good deep tire trood!!\n• You may have to let some air out your fires to \'Acar\' in the deep sand.\n• Head rorth un road 102. After 3 miles and after the cattle gourd, you will drop down into lunge dry\nwash.\n• Turn left in the wash froad 105HI and park or the entrance to the slot canyon.\n• Look for the \'Mozui Steps, a series of steps packed into the canyon walls by the early Anasazi whe\nlived in the cran. These steps lead to a grannry above, where com and other supplies were stored.\n(Pictured bottom left).\n• When returning, you can use road \"02M, which wil drop you onto the Best Friends paved road.\n• Hire one of our several gu des and outlitters to take you to Peekaboo.\nDISCLAIMER:\n106C\nGPS 37 10.676\n112 33.564\nPEEKABOO\nSLOT\nCANYON\n35 mia,\nWARNING:\n724\nAPI\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dit roads are impassable when wat. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water,\nfood. sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the \'rack art\'. Leave no trace of your visit so\nothers may enjoy.\"\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 S 100 E\nVERY DEEP SAND\n9 mi\nA\nMILE\n7\n2\nHIGH CLEARANCE FWD REQUIRED\nCONSIDER HIRING A GUIDE\nHIKING MOT RECOMMENDED\nYES\nDEEP SAND\n02997\n55497\nHALF DAY\nan\n5525 FEET\n102\ncanyon opens up\nkeep on going to\nthe next section\nof the canyon\nSome maps call this \"Red Canyon,\" but\nthe locals know it as \"Peekaboo\' even\nthough there are several Southern Utah\nslot canyons that bear the same name.\naurs is the BESTI Many photographers\nrefer to this beauty as \"Antelope\nCanyon without the crowds\"! Slot\ncanyons are formed by eons of swift\nwater rushing through sandstone rock,\ncarrying along with it rocks, trees, anc\nanything else that may be in the path.\nLook clorg the canyon walls, and you\ncan tell how high the water level has\nbeen recently. There are two sections\nto the canyon, so make sure you hike\nto the end for the full experience.\n102 M\nEASIER ROUTE\n106J\nL\nDROP INTO THE WASH 102J\nCATTLE GUARD\n3019\n102\nLIFE\ntread lightly! UTAH\nELEVATED\nOn\nDEEP SAND\n102L\nSHUBIDY\nKANAB\nMERICALLY UNSPOILER\nAPP\n102\nN\n3.5 mi\nExerc\nKANAB\nNasa POL','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Peekaboo Slot Canyon\",\n  \"distance\": \"9 miles\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year-round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Moderate\",\n  \"elevation\": \"5,525 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.176\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-112.564\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"High clearance vehicle required\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"No\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"Half day\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"ATV\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"About 9 miles north from Kanab on HWY 89 between milepost 72 and 73, you will see the turn off for Peekaboo trailhead on the east side of the road. The road into the canyon is a deep sandy trail that requires good deep tire tread. You may have to let some air out of your tires to increase traction in the deep sand. Head north on road 102. After 3 miles and after the cattle guard, you will drop down into a dry wash. Turn left in the wash onto road 105HI and park at the entrance to the slot canyon. Look for the \'Mozui Steps,\' a series of steps packed into the canyon walls by the early Anasazi who lived in the area. When returning, you can use road 102M, which will drop you onto the Best Friends paved road. Consider hiring a guide to take you to Peekaboo.\",\n  \"description\": \"Peekaboo Slot Canyon, also known as Red Canyon, is a beautiful slot canyon located in southern Utah. It offers a unique hiking experience without the crowds found in other popular slot canyons like Antelope Canyon. The canyon was formed by swift water rushing through sandstone rock over millions of years. Look along the canyon walls to see the water level markings. There are two sections to the canyon, so make sure to hike all the way to the end for the full experience.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Peekaboo Slot Canyon, also known as Red Canyon, is a beautiful slot canyon located in southern Utah. It offers a unique hiking experience without the crowds found in other popular slot canyons like Antelope Canyon. The canyon was formed by swift water rushing through sandstone rock over millions of years. Look along the canyon walls to see the water level markings. There are two sections to the canyon, so make sure to hike all the way to the end for the full experience.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads may be impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas. Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:36:05','2023-09-22 02:42:18'),(43,'trails',298,'PONDEROSA GROVE\nCAMPGROUND\nADVENTURE MAP\nAXA\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nCORAL PINK SAND DUNES\nSTATE PARK\nBEST SEASON:\nМОТ ЗА\nYEAR ROUND\nEXPOSURE SUN AND SHADE TREES\nCAMPING: TENTS AND SMALL CAMPERS\nNOTE: MAXIMUM 24 FT TRIALER SIZE\nDIFFICULTY: EASY FAMILY FRIENDLY\nELEVATION:\nPONDEROSA GROVE\nCAMPGROUND/PICNICKING/OHV TRAILS\nGETTING THERE:\n• From Kanab, travel & miles north on HWY 39.\n• Just past mile post 72, turn left cnto Hancock road.\n• Drive opproximately 7.5 miles, watch for the Ponderosa Grave Recreation Site sign\ncnc turn right.\nNO\n• The compground consists of nire indivicual campstes ard a group site,\npicnic tables, concrete fire rings, barbecue grills and pit toilets.\n• The sites are spread far enough apart, between Ponderosa Pines to ensure privacy.\n• There is a fee per site per night\n• Bring your own water and firewood.\nCAMPGROUND\n6300 FEET\nDISCLAIMER:\nThis map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designared roads. Dirt roads are impassable when wet. Please respect\nPrivate Propery. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water,\nfood. sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is nonexistent in most creast\nDo not remove anifacts or deface the \'rock ort\'. leave no trace of your visit so\nothers may enjoy.\"\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 785 100 E\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\n7.5 mi IN\nPONDEROSA\nGROVE\nSOUTH FORK\nINDIAN CANYON\nPICTOGRAPHS\nHELL DIVE\nPICTOGRAFHB\nIf you are camping and want an\naffordable, quiet, yot primitive\ncampsite, check out Ponderosa\nGrove. This campground is ideally\nlocated near the north side of the\nCoral Pink Sand Dunes State Park,\nand is accassec by pavec roads.\nThe campground is well\nmaintained with a gravel loop.\nand can accommodate tents and\nsmall campers less than 24 ft. The\ncampsites are in a ponderosa\nforest and provide a scenic locale\nfor travelers, OTV enthusiasts,\ncompers and family. This region\nis perfect for exploring the great\noutdoors and is a quiet place to\nrelax and have a picnic\nHANCOCK ROAD\nLIFE\ntread lightly! UTAH\nMILE\nWW\n7.8 mi\nKANAB\nMAGICALLY USPOILE\nUT\nN\nBand\n(89)\nKANAB\nKANAB\nKABILLY UPULES','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Ponderosa Grove Campground\",\n  \"distance\": \"\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year Round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n  \"elevation\": \"6300 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": \"\",\n  \"longitude\": \"\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"Accessible via paved roads\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"Unknown\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, travel 7 miles north on HWY 39. Just past mile post 72, turn left onto Hancock road. Drive approximately 7.5 miles, watch for the Ponderosa Grove Recreation Site sign and turn right.\",\n  \"description\": \"If you are camping and want an affordable, quiet, yet primitive campsite, check out Ponderosa Grove Campground. This campground is ideally located near the north side of the Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park and is accessible by paved roads. The campground is well maintained with a gravel loop and can accommodate tents and small campers less than 24 ft. The campsites are surrounded by ponderosa pines, providing a scenic locale for travelers, OHV enthusiasts, campers, and families. This region is perfect for exploring the great outdoors and is a quiet place to relax and have a picnic.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>If you are camping and want an affordable, quiet, yet primitive campsite, check out Ponderosa Grove Campground. This campground is ideally located near the north side of the Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park and is accessible by paved roads. The campground is well maintained with a gravel loop and can accommodate tents and small campers less than 24 ft. The campsites are surrounded by ponderosa pines, providing a scenic locale for travelers, OHV enthusiasts, campers, and families. This region is perfect for exploring the great outdoors and is a quiet place to relax and have a picnic.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"The campground consists of nine individual campsites and a group site with picnic tables, concrete fire rings, barbecue grills, and pit toilets. The sites are spread far enough apart between Ponderosa Pines to ensure privacy. There is a fee per site per night. Bring your own water and firewood.\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:36:21','2023-09-22 02:42:36'),(44,'trails',299,'RAVEN/ROADRUNNER\nBIKE/HIKE\n300.\nRAVEN\n1.21 mi o\nDIY\nHod\nP\nPARRY\nLODCE\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nSQUAW\nTRAIL\n1.4 mi\nBEST SEASON:\nBIKING:\nHIKING:\nAVERAGE TIME:\nPETS:\nELEVATION:\nCanyon\nYEAR ROUND\nEASY\nA FEW HOURS\nPET FRIENDLY ON LEASH\n.\nNO\nMODERATE\nGETTING THERE!\n• Start at the center of town and head north on 100 East.\n• When you get to the bend in the road by Farry Lodge stay right on 100 East.\n.\n5040-5800 FEET\nTV TOWER\nPROADRUNNER\n93 mi\n• Behind the ball fields you will see the trailhead for the Squaw Trail.\n.\n• Follow Squaw trail until you see the sign on your right for the Roadrunrer trail.\n.\n• There is additional parking if you head west along the back of the ball fields and on\nthe other side of the dike.\n• Carry plenty of water and sun protection.\nEnjoy these awesome bike loops.\nDISCLAIMER:\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads cre mpassable when wel. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water\nfood, sunscreen, and suppies Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your vist so\nothers may enjoy.\"\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 5 100 E\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\nSQUAW TRAIL\nDry\nSpring\nRoven/Roadrunner is a short mountain\nbike challenge in the heart of Kanah,\nbut you may choose to hike it. This is\nthe first completed section of an\nextensive planned mourtain bike trail\nsystem. It is best to do this trail\nclockwise.\nms\nSavano\nPoint\nDescription Intermediate and.\nexperienced evel mountain bikers\nwill enjoy these trails winding through\nred rock and beautiful landscapes.\nThis would also be a fun treil for a\nfam ly hike, Bikers and hikers will find\nthe trailhend just west of Squaw Trail\nnorth of Karab City\'s Jacob Homblin\nPark. There are many hikes that start\nfrom the Squaw Trail\nRAVEN/ROADRUNNER\norta\nmilion\nΚΑΝΑΒ\nLIFE\nADVENTURE MAP tread lightly! UTAH\nELEVATED\nChiffs\n185\nKANAB\nMAGICALLY UNSPOILE\nANTIZA\nAPP\nBIKE/HIKE\nTOMS CANYON,\nPUGH CANYON\nToms\n5800\nKANAB\nMERILTISPLICED\n$8','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Raven/Roadrunner\",\n  \"distance\": \"1.21 mi\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n  \"elevation\": \"5040-5800 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": null,\n  \"longitude\": null,\n  \"accessibility\": \"DIY\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"Pet friendly on leash\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"A few hours\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"Bike/Hike\",\n  \"getting_there\": [\n    \"Start at the center of town and head north on 100 East.\",\n    \"When you get to the bend in the road by Farry Lodge, stay right on 100 East.\",\n    \"Behind the ball fields you will see the trailhead for the Squaw Trail.\",\n    \"Follow Squaw trail until you see the sign on your right for the Roadrunner trail.\",\n    \"There is additional parking if you head west along the back of the ball fields and on the other side of the dike.\"\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"Raven/Roadrunner is a short mountain bike challenge in the heart of Kanab, but you may choose to hike it. This is the first completed section of an extensive planned mountain bike trail system. It is best to do this trail clockwise. Intermediate and experienced level mountain bikers will enjoy these trails winding through red rock and beautiful landscapes. This would also be a fun trail for a family hike. Bikers and hikers will find the trailhead just west of Squaw Trail north of Kanab City\'s Jacob Hamblin Park. There are many hikes that start from the Squaw Trail.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Raven/Roadrunner is a short mountain bike challenge in the heart of Kanab, but you may choose to hike it. This is the first completed section of an extensive planned mountain bike trail system. It is best to do this trail clockwise. Intermediate and experienced level mountain bikers will enjoy these trails winding through red rock and beautiful landscapes. This would also be a fun trail for a family hike. Bikers and hikers will find the trailhead just west of Squaw Trail north of Kanab City\'s Jacob Hamblin Park. There are many hikes that start from the Squaw Trail.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": {\n    \"disclaimer\": \"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads can become impassable when wet. Please respect Private Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas. Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\",\n    \"visitor_center\": {\n      \"address\": \"78 5 100 E\",\n      \"phone\": \"435.644.5033\"\n    }\n  }\n}','2023-09-10 06:36:29','2023-09-22 02:43:00'),(45,'trails',300,'Laim\nSAND D