ting to this location.\nWhen you arrive at Warriors Walk you will\nsce inspiring scenery and sandstone sickrock\nwith views of Zion in the background. It is\nuncertain who left this pathway across the\nsandstore. Could it be the Native American\nPeople who left a hail lined with rocks hrough\nthe deser? No ane is aluin Bring a cumeru,\nyou won\'t want to miss this photo opportunity.\nIf you have time you can also visit the Mail\nCrop or explore the many trails in the area.\n25D\nV\nK2150\n20\nELEPHANT BUTTE ELEPHANT GAP\nK 1260 20\nLIFE\nUTAH\nELEVATED\n20\n25\n20\n20\n[20]\nK1255 P\nKANAB\nMAGICALLY UNSPOILE\nN\n62 SAND DUNES\nPATINE\nUT\nAPP\nELEPHANT COVE\nSTAGING AREA\nKANAB\nMG CALLE ESPOILED','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Warriors Walk\",\n  \"distance\": 19,\n  \"best_season\": \"All year round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Moderate\",\n  \"elevation\": 5771,\n  \"latitude\": 37.3289,\n  \"longitude\": -112.7177,\n  \"accessibility\": \"Yes\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"Yes\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": 5,\n  \"vehicle\": \"ATV/JEEP\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, drive 7.8 miles north on HWY 89. Just past mile post 71, turn left onto the Hancock road. Drive 9.3 miles to the stop sign and turn left. Drive 9.1 miles and turn right on road K1250 it is also signed 13200 West. Drive 2.2 miles to sign with road map. You can park here and unload ATV\'s. The trail starts on your left. Drive 4.7 miles and turn left on road 17. Drive approximately 2 miles, stay right on road 19. At about 2.5 miles, turn left on road 19A. The road will end, park here. Look at that view of Zion!!!\",\n  \"description\": \"Warriors Walk is a popular OHV ride for Kane County locals. The ride starts 4 miles west of the Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park and heads north past Elephant Butte. The ride is mostly sandy trails winding through sagebrush and juniper trees, with a few sections of sandstone. Getting here can be challenging. Larger 4WD vehicles will have a difficult time getting to this location. When you arrive at Warriors Walk, you will see inspiring scenery and sandstone slickrock with views of Zion in the background. It is uncertain who left this pathway across the sandstone. Could it be the Native American people who left a trail lined with rocks through the desert? No one knows for sure. Bring a camera, you won\'t want to miss this photo opportunity. If you have time, you can also visit the Mail Drop or explore the many trails in the area.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Warriors Walk is a popular OHV ride for Kane County locals. The ride starts 4 miles west of the Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park and heads north past Elephant Butte. The ride is mostly sandy trails winding through sagebrush and juniper trees, with a few sections of sandstone. Getting here can be challenging. Larger 4WD vehicles will have a difficult time getting to this location. When you arrive at Warriors Walk, you will see inspiring scenery and sandstone slickrock with views of Zion in the background. It is uncertain who left this pathway across the sandstone. Could it be the Native American people who left a trail lined with rocks through the desert? No one knows for sure. Bring a camera, you won\'t want to miss this photo opportunity. If you have time, you can also visit the Mail Drop or explore the many trails in the area.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads may be impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas! Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit.\",\n  \"telephone\": \"435.644.5033\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:38:03','2023-09-22 02:46:33'),(56,'trails',311,'WHITE POCKET\nHIGH CLEARANCE 4WD\nWHITE POCKET\nHIGH CLEARANCE 4WD\nN\nKANAB 38.6 mi.\nMONT\nADVENTURE MAP\n(89\nOF