of a long list of stunning\nformations the area has to offer. Locals\npreler White Pocket, a much larger area\nthen The Wove. A moonscape like\nlandscase hat requires no permit! The\nswiring twisted, multi colored natural\nartwork of White Pocke, will fill your senses\nbeyond imagination. Get an early start, as\nthis is an all day adventure. A 4WD, high\nclearance vehicle is a must for this journey,\nor hire a locul guide to take you out. This is\nan adventure you don\'t want to miss\n5.6 mi\n1086\n3.9 mi.\n111 57.692\"\n36 50.604.\nWA\nLIFE\ntread lightly! UTAH\nELEVATED\n11154.111)\n36 56 242\nKANAB\nMOGICALLY USPOILE\nVETUL\nUT KANAB\nKACHLY USPORED','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"White Pocket\",\n  \"distance\": \"N/A\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year Round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Easy Hike/Deep Sand\",\n  \"elevation\": \"5673 Feet\",\n  \"latitude\": \"36.93734\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-111.957692\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"High Clearance 4WD\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"Yes\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"Full Day\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"4WD / ATV\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, drive 38.6 miles east on HWY 89. Between milepost 26 and 25, you will see a dirt road that heads south. This is House Rock Valley Road, generally a very well-maintained hard packed dirt road. At 20.3 miles, turn left onto Road 1017 at the horse corral. From this point, high clearance, 4WD vehicles are required. Park and unload your ATV here. Let some air out of your tires to navigate the sandy terrain. Travel 6.2 miles on Road 1017. At the junction, continue straight on Road 1087. Drive 3.9 miles and stay left on Road 1036. Continue on Road 1086 for 5.6 miles to The White Pocket trailhead. Park at the trailhead and begin your short hike.\",\n  \"description\": \"Many visitors come to Southern Utah to do The Wave, one of the most photographed rock formations in the world! Unfortunately, due to its fragile nature, permits are limited to a maximum of 64 hikers a day. Many don\'t realize that The Wave is only the beginning of a long list of stunning formations the area has to offer. Locals prefer White Pocket, a much larger area than The Wave. A moonscape-like landscape that requires no permit. The swirling twisted, multi-colored natural artwork of White Pocket will fill your senses beyond imagination. Get an early start, as this is an all-day adventure. A 4WD, high clearance vehicle is a must for this journey, or hire a local guide to take you out. This is an adventure you don\'t want to miss!\",\n  \"description_html\": \"Many visitors come to Southern Utah to do The Wave, one of the most photographed rock formations in the world! Unfortunately, due to its fragile nature, permits are limited to a maximum of 64 hikers a day. Many don\'t realize that The Wave is only the beginning of a long list of stunning formations the area has to offer. Locals prefer White Pocket, a much larger area than The Wave. A moonscape-like landscape that requires no permit. The swirling twisted, multi-colored natural artwork of White Pocket will fill your senses beyond imagination. Get an early start, as this is an all-day adventure. A 4WD, high clearance vehicle is a must for this journey, or hire a local guide to take you out. This is an adventure you don\'t want to miss!\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"NOTE: Much of White Pocket is privately ranched. Please respect the privacy of others. Please do not disturb their property and animals.\\n\\nDISCLAIMER: This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads are impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas! Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\\n\\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 785 100 E\\